{"id":"pam_shells.8","n":"pam_shells","s":"8","src":{"r":{"pkg":"pam","ver":"1.5.1-26.el9_6","repo":"BaseOS","url":"https://dl.rockylinux.org/vault/rocky/9.6/BaseOS/x86_64/os/Packages/p/pam-1.5.1-26.el9_6.x86_64.rpm","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/pam_shells.8.gz","sha256":"0eb9874591978c4b224b28d963933aeae99ecc8301fede1b366e059e21d8c1c1","date":"11/25/2020","origin":"Linux-PAM Manual"},"u":{"pkg":"libpam-modules","ver":"1.4.0-11ubuntu2.8","repo":"jammy-updates/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/p/pam/libpam-modules_1.4.0-11ubuntu2.8_amd64.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/pam_shells.8.gz","sha256":"5dea19867b356853b5d47d75ddf5e1ee240da12d6e897fadcdaec618a5737b2b","date":"06/08/2020","origin":"Linux-PAM Manual"}},"nopt":{"r":0,"u":0},"desc":"PAM module to check for valid login shell","same":false,"r":[["NAME","<p>pam_shells - PAM module to check for valid login shell</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>pam_shells.so</b></p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p>pam_shells is a PAM module that only allows access to the system if the user's shell is listed in /etc/shells.</p> <p>It also checks if /etc/shells is a plain file and not world writable.</p>"],["OPTIONS","<p>This module does not recognise any options.</p>"],["MODULE TYPES PROVIDED","<p>The <b>auth</b> and <b>account</b> module types are provided.</p>"],["RETURN VALUES","<p>PAM_AUTH_ERR</p> <div class=\"in\">Access to the system was denied.</div> <p>PAM_SUCCESS</p> <div class=\"in\">The user's login shell was listed as valid shell in /etc/shells.</div> <p>PAM_SERVICE_ERR</p> <div class=\"in\">The module was not able to get the name of the user.</div>"],["EXAMPLES","<div class=\"in\"> <pre>auth  required  pam_shells.so\n<br>\n      </pre> </div>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>shells</b>(5), <b>pam.conf</b>(5), <b>pam.d</b>(5), <b>pam</b>(8)</p>"],["AUTHOR","<p>pam_shells was written by Erik Troan &lt;ewt@redhat.com&gt;.</p>"]],"u":[["NAME",0],["SYNOPSIS",1],["DESCRIPTION",2],["OPTIONS",3],["MODULE TYPES PROVIDED",4],["RETURN VALUES",5],["EXAMPLES",6],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>shells</b>(5), <b>pam.conf</b>(5), <b>pam.d</b>(5), <b>pam</b>(7)</p>"],["AUTHOR",8]],"diff":{"r":[],"u":[]}}